ase, the archive and the corpus ($0): per item the routing, the model's raw answer with what the code dropped and why, every matching decision with the model's reason, what was written, the day's judging, and a rule-based diagnosis (空手 / 全被丢 / 杂音多 / 多为重复 / 正常); the item's text, the request as the model saw it and the raw answer are files next to it. Reading it, Alex asked for the corpus labels to be tightened before any rerun ("扫描一次 tag 需要收紧的地方……先别帮我重跑"): ten rules in `poc/corpus/scripts/assemble.py` (my census found three: Commerce Federal Register notices carry no object, certification and policy exhibits are 不算材料, an aggregator page's author is the byline's outlet; a Codex read-only review found seven more: peer themes only on results/reports/calls, the issuing agency as the official publisher, copies across kinds, the 8-K Item 2.02 body not the table of contents, 6-K covers, video pages not full, the newsroom results rule, plus author-table additions), each with controls in `poc/corpus/scripts/test_labels.py`, applied by `poc/corpus/scripts/relabel.py` to a copy of the frozen corpus as `poc/data/items-window-tags2-2026-10-24.sqlite` (routed items in the range 584 → 480; the frozen file and the sealed results untouched). The one disagreement (whether Commerce anti-dumping notices on Chinese goods belong to the 中美关税 theme) was settled on 2026-10-24 by Alex's thesis test: none of the 89 China notices touches the chip or server supply chain and no thesis cites them, so the rule stays (`docs/poc/pipeline-plan.md`). Open defect: the official harvest's file names collided (97 notices, 56 with another notice's body; naming fixed in `harvest_official.py`, re-fetch needed before the next corpus build). Census, review and dispositions: `docs/poc/pipeline-plan.md`, `docs/research/2026-10-24-corpus-tags/`. No rerun has been started. The front-end mock is now a generated page backed by the modular Thesis UI in `poc/ui/` (D130): a versioned JSON schema, one adapter for existing bundles, pure dated model selectors, and separate card, chart, evidence, select, disclosure, canvas and detail components. The 22-line `poc/mock/index.template.html` is only the page shell; `scripts/mock_build.py` validates the data and bundles the modules into the standalone `poc/mock/index.html`. Agreed UI decisions D64–D129 are preserved. Card-native hover titles are removed (D131). The Thesis detail drawer slides in and out over 280ms with a fading scrim; interrupted motion reverses, and teardown cancels it (D136). Seven browser checks cover both directions, focus return, reversal, data replacement and teardown; X, Escape and scrim closes are verified. Connector routing is now shared in `poc/ui/src/components/connectors.js` (D137). The stored 12-branch graph has no overlapping routes; 94 fan-out sizes pass geometry checks, and browser checks confirm attached endpoints for 4, 12 and 41 branches, including zoom and range redraw. Scratch mutations restoring the shared lane or unbounded ports fail those checks. The Idea card and graph are corrected under D138: a shared 40px header, no duplicate decomposition rows, all chosen theses directly connected to the Idea, and related theses attached to their supplied source. The stored three-part response contains eight chosen and five related theses; all 13 edges and 14 headers were checked in the browser, including empty/null replies and a range redraw. Both the first-only-root and wrong-related-parent mutations are rejected. All 19 UI tests and 32 Python tests pass. Components use scoped DOM ids and event cleanup and accept data/callbacks; they do not call a model. `src/hivemind/bundle.py` supplies stable assessment ids and event dates; `thesis_bundles` (MCP) and `GET /thesis-bundles?ids=...` expose the same complete read-only input. Data arrives through `fromBundles` or `fromIdeaResponse` and becomes the immutable `thesis-ui/1` contract. Invalid payloads are rejected before replacing the current screen. The preserved local Idea matching and number control live in `poc/ui/src/legacy/idea.js`; Idea product behavior and the live LLM overlay remain the next UI task, explicitly deferred by Alex. Integration and commands: `poc/ui/README.md`; design and tables: `docs/poc/thesis-ui.md`. Verification: 10 UI tests, three rejected date-related mutants, and the full 31-test Python suite pass; the HTTP and MCP bundle routes were exercised through their real transports without model calls. Browser checks cover two concurrent component instances, invalid updates, teardown/recreation, empty history, date selection, replay, type filtering and the retained visuals. The final JS bundle is about 174 KB; the 42-thesis demo validates in about 23 ms on this machine. In the evening Alex reset the POC's direction (D76): Hivemind is a database with a search engine on top, packaged as MCP and HTTP; the caller searches, chooses and arranges views itself. Built: `src/hivemind/service.py` (as-of reads: views, view, history, evidence, record, changes, evaluate), `src/hivemind/search.py` (embedding index over each view's own text in `poc/data/search-index.sqlite`, cosine + object and text boosts, lexical fallback), `scripts/hivemind_mcp.py` (9 tools, stdio), `scripts/hivemind_api.py` (127.0.0.1), `scripts/search_eval.py`, tests in `tests/` (21 passing on the sealed ledger, including the HTTP front started as a user starts it); design in `docs/poc/service.md`. Codex's read-only review (`docs/research/2026-10-24-service/`) found eight defects, all reproduced and fixed with a failing test each (dispositions in `disposition.md`): the threaded HTTP server crossing SQLite threads, relationships and cited sources leaking from after `as_of`, the band parser misreading 18 money ladders (rewritten), "=" misjudged, stale vectors ranked as semantic, the eval script's `none` and exit code, the embedding error echoing the response body. A second Codex pass on the fixes found six more (a float conversion moving v84's boundary